The  file  is  a  simplified version of the data base used to de‐
scribe terminal lines.  The initial terminal  login  process  ac‐
cesses  the file each time it starts, allowing simpler reconfigu‐
ration of terminal characteristics.  Each entry in the data  base
is  used  to  describe  one  class  of  terminals.   Where to run
processes is normally defined by  There  is  a  default  terminal
class, that is used to set global defaults for all other classes.
(That  is,  the  entry  is read, then the entry for the class re‐
quired is used to override particular settings.)   The  entry  is
also  normally  read by other programs that present login prompts
to the user, such as in order to retrieve the values of  the  and
capabilities.   Refer  to  for  a description of the file layout.
